     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg per day in total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- **500 to 1,000 mg twice daily**, the usual dosing, with a lower starting dose if the patient is new to metformin\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical reason. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
